    "vision": {
      "answer": "The chart encodes three opinion components—positive (P), negative (N), and uncertainty (U), which sum to 1—through each observation’s position in the ternary plot. Customer gender is encoded by color: teal for none/unspecified, yellow for male, and lavender for female; the heights of the surrounding radial bars encode the number of customers in each opinion region.",
